<title>USA: Fluke stake cut by Philips to 6.6pct.</title>
<headline>Fluke stake cut by Philips to 6.6pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philips Electronics N.V. said Tuesday it cut its stake in Fluke Corp to 6.6 percent from about 7.8 percent.</p>
<p>In a filing with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission, Philips said it sold 102,500 shares of Fluke between October 29 and November 7 at prices ranging from $38 to $40 each.</p>
<p>The Netherlands-based electronic company said it still held its stake in Fluke, an Everett, Wash.,-based maker of industrial testing products, for investment purposes.</p>
</text>
